  "category": "revenue",
  "description": "Realized LTV (Lifetime Value) per Paying Customer (also known as Average Revenue per Paying User, ARPPU) measures the actual (gross) revenue that was generated by a customer cohort, divided by the number of paying customers in that cohort. It gives you an overall view of how paid customer cohorts monetize over time.\nCustomers are cohorted by the date they were first seen, i.e. the date they first opened your app. Using the \u201cCustomer Lifetime\u201d selector, you can define the time period after the customer was first seen that should be included in the LTV calculation. For example, by setting the \u201cCustomer Lifetime\u201d selector to 30 days, only revenue generated by new paying customers in their first 30 days will be included.\n\nRealized LTV per Paying Customer can be used as a tool to understand the profitability of (paid) acquisition, compare the impact of product price changes over time, and much more.",
